  "label": "User projected onto the textual message addressing 'ladies' and 'your man'",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material that directly addresses 'ladies!' and 'your man', creating an implicit 'you' (the viewer) who is being instructed to evaluate their partner's reaction to the image. The text 'ladies! if your man is offended by this' explicitly directs the user's attention and judgment toward their own partner, making the viewer a participant in the meme's social commentary. This projection is onto the textual material, which frames the user as the one who should assess their partner's masculinity based on their reaction to the dog-fighting scene.",
